note Linux x86_64 open flags (asm-generic/fcntl.h): O_DIRECTORY 0200000 = 65536, O_NOFOLLOW 0400000 =
note 131072, O_CLOEXEC 02000000 = 524288, O_WRONLY 1, O_CREAT 64, O_EXCL 128, O_TRUNC 512. The stat
note words of omc's x86linux backend write the AArch64 layout (st_mode at 16, st_size at 48), not the
note x86_64 kernel layout (mode at 24): observed 2026-11-11 with omc 3ad9f10f under qemu-x86_64, the
note same 144 bytes from lstat of one file under both targets (tools/bring/PLATFORMS.md).
fn pl_oflag how ulong to int
if eq how 1
ret 720896
end
if eq how 2
ret 655937
end
if eq how 3
ret 655553
end
if eq how 4
ret 524288
end
ret 655360
end
fn pl_mode b view uchar * to ulong
ret rd32 b 16
end
fn pl_size b view uchar * to ulong
ret rd64 b 48
end
